          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness reports in 2013 observing in August 1998 at 1:30 AM a luminous phenomenon, like a flash lasting one or two seconds at most, displaying all colors across the entire sky. The witness's sister also saw the phenomenon. Only one testimony is reported. This testimony is not exploitable by GEIPAN as it is an observation reported 15 years after the facts without specifying the date of the observation. The observation is not unusual, as it resembles a meteoroid atmospheric re-entry flash, but it is impossible to investigate further in this direction. Consequently, GEIPAN classifies this case as C: lack of information.",
